<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Score</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> score [group|hp|ep|mp]
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre> <a cmd='#'>score</a>
 <a cmd='#'>score hp</a>
 <a cmd='#'>score group</a>
</pre>
<p>When you're playing, you might want to know what your current condition is.
For this, you use the command 'score'. Then the game states your current
hitpoints, mana points, and endurance points as well as other useful 
information.
</p><p>It is possible to simply get your hp, ep or mp as a single number by using
the command e.g. <a cmd='#'>score hp</a>.
</p><p>The <a cmd='#'>score group</a> command is useful when you're in a group to see how your
fellow players are doing.
</p><p>While you are fighting, only <a cmd='#'>score hp</a>, <a cmd='#'>score ep</a> and <a cmd='#'>score mp</a> work. Until
you have saved for the first time (see <a cmd='#'>Help Save</a>), score and score group
only tell you that you are still a guest.
</p><p>See Also:
</p>
<pre> &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Prompt</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Status</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Hitpoints</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Mana Points</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Endurance</a>
</pre>




</div>